<div class="exercise"><div class="ex-q"><p>Why might two different state-space models with the same transfer function still behave differently in a simulation that starts from non-zero initial conditions?</p>
</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class="ex-s"><p>They don’t, if they’re related by a similarity transform and you transform the initial state too. But a model can also contain uncontrollable or unobservable modes that cancel in the transfer function; those modes respond to initial conditions even though the transfer function hides them. Minimal realisations have none.</p>
</div></details></div>
